  "description": "Plane Trees \rP6 and P4: Prune back touching branches by 1 to 2 metres maximum (small diameter growth). \rP2 and P4 : Prune back touching branches by 1 to 2 metres maximum (small diameter growth). \rP3 and P5:  Prune back touching branches by 1 to 2 metres maximum (small diameter growth).  \rP5: Prune back from maple by 1 to 2 metres maximum (small diameter growth). \rP7: Prune back from maple by 1 to 2 metres maximum (small diameter growth) and reduce lower branch \rof maple by 1 to 2 metres. \rP8 and P10: Prune back touching branches by 1 to 2 metres maximum (small diameter growth). \rP14 and P15: Thin branch ends to allow additional light penetration. \rP11 and P12: Thin branch ends to allow additional light penetration through both trees. P9 and P6 Thin branch ends to allow additional light penetration through both trees. \rAll plane trees to have crowns lifted to approximately 5.5 metres, removing longer drooping branches whilst maintaining the natural flow and appearance of the tree line.",
